  "result": "Here's a first draft (about 90 words):\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nCarrier rate cards are in `shop/carriers/`, one module per carrier (`acme.py`\nthrough `tundra.py`). Each one is registered in `shop/carriers/__init__.py`, and\nyou can fetch it by name with `carriers.get(\"acme\")`.\n\nEvery carrier module defines `BASE_RATE`, a flat charge in cents. It also\ndefines a per-weight rate and a weight limit. A carrier's `rate(weight, zone)`\nreturns the quote in cents.\n\nMost carriers take weight in kilograms (`PER_KG`, `MAX_KG`). **Maple** is the\nexception: it takes weight in **grams** (`PER_GRAMS`, `MAX_GRAMS = 30000`), so\npass `rate()` grams, not kg.\n```\n\nI checked this against the carrier modules: all 20 define `BASE_RATE`, and `maple.py` is the only one that uses grams. I haven't changed `README.md`. Do you want me to add the section under the existing intro?",
